    "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`BeamSearchParams` accepted `max_tokens=0` (or negative) without any validation, while `SamplingParams` rejects `max_tokens < 1` with `VLLMValidationError`.\r\n\r\nWith an unvalidated value, `beam_search()` silently misbehaves instead of raising:\r\n- the offline path (`LLM.beam_search`) skips the generation loop and returns the prompt echoed back as generated text;\r\n- the online path yields an empty completion with `finish_reason=\"length\"`.\r\n\r\nThis change adds the same `max_tokens >= 1` check to `BeamSearchParams.__post_init__`, mirroring `SamplingParams._verify_args`.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- New unit test `test_beam_search_params_rejects_non_positive_max_tokens` in `tests/test_sampling_params.py`: asserts `VLLMValidationError` for `max_tokens` in `(0, -1, -100)` and acceptance of `1` and `16`.\r\n- Verified no in-tree callers or tests construct `BeamSearchParams` with `max_tokens < 1` (existing tests use values >= 1; internal beam-search engine calls use `max_tokens=1`), so no existing behavior changes.\r\n",
